<title>UK: BICC to form optical cable j/v with Corning.</title>
<headline>BICC to form optical cable j/v with Corning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>BICC Plc, the cables and construction group, said on Monday it had signed a joint venture agreement with Corning for the development of a regional optical cable business in Asia-Pacific.  </p>
<p>BICC said the business would be called BICCOR Pte Ltd and be 60 percent owned by BICC Cables Asia-Pacific and 40 percent by Corning Inc.</p>
<p>BICC Cables Asia-Pacific is a 50/50 joint venture between BICC plc and Metal Manufactures Ltd of Australia, of which BICC is the majority owner.</p>
<p>BICC and Corning are already partners in Optical Fibres, based in Deeside, north Wales.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
